MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Beatles 1 and Elvis 30 #1 Hits fit my repeated interest in greatest-hits collections: familiar songs gathered together are appealing next choices.",
    "Rumours fits the melodic classic rock I have been exploring through The Cars and classic-rock collections, while Revolver and Let It Be connect naturally to my interest in Sgt. Pepper."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "American Idiot, Mer De Noms and The Sickness lean toward punk or heavier rock; sharing a broad rock connection does not give me the familiar, melodic listening experience I want now.",
    "On How Life Is feels less connected to my current interest in older rock and retrospective hits. PTXmas connects to my recent Christmas listening, but that alone does not tell me whether I will enjoy its vocal style."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in classic rock seems to have been stretched into an interest in rock of very different sounds and intensity.",
    "My Beatles interest supports several relevant suggestions, but it does not mean I want to choose several Beatles releases in the same session."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The repeated greatest-hits and best-of titles in my history matter: I am often drawn to collections of familiar songs rather than exploring another full album immediately.",
    "My latest Christmas album makes seasonal music relevant, but my longer pattern of older hits and melodic classic rock still matters when deciding what I would actually choose."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in Beatles music and older hits, but stretched that interest too far toward heavier rock and treated some relevant options as more immediately appealing than they felt to me."
}
